# Revocation (NON-MEMBERSHIP) statement of a KVAC credential lifecycle.
#
# Claim proved: "My secret 12-byte revocation value is NOT present in the
# public revocation tree (root %root), so my credential has not been revoked."
# The prover demonstrates non-membership via an adjacent record whose half-open
# interval [low, hi) strictly straddles the target: low < target < hi.  The
# record sits at a secret position in the indexed Merkle tree, authenticated by
# the sibling path %sib and the secret per-level directions %dirs.
#
# Lifecycle: while the value is absent, some adjacent record straddles it and a
# non-revocation proof exists.  Once the value is inserted (revoked), the IMT is
# split exactly at the target, so the target becomes a record value and NO
# adjacent interval strictly straddles it anymore: the non-revocation proof
# becomes impossible.  A stale pre-revocation witness no longer matches the new
# root and is rejected.  See example_shipshape_kvac for the full arc and
# example_shipshape_anon_membership for the membership building block.
#
# Indexed leaf layout (hirose_fixed_32): each IMT leaf record is
#   value(12) || next_value(12) || next_index(8) = 32 bytes,
# exactly the fixed 32-byte single-block hirose leaf.  That FREEZES the field
# widths: value/next_value are 12 bytes and next_index is 8 bytes here, NOT 32.
# Comparisons are little-endian (byte 0 = LSB) per the assert_lt convention, so
# the target must be strictly between the empty set bounds (not all 0x00, not
# all 0xFF).
#
# Privacy model: target, low, hi, nidx, the sibling path, and the per-level
# directions are ALL witness (private).  Only the revocation root is public
# (INSTANCE).  The construction takes the root as an INSTANCE input and asserts
# the path internally (like ring_sig/v1): there is no ASSERT_EQUAL block.
#
# Tree shape: depth 8 (256-record IMT).  Node width is fixed at 32 bytes by
# hirose_fixed_32, so depth scales by changing only %sib (byte[D * 32]) and
# %dirs (byte[D]); the value/index widths and %root stay fixed.  ext
# (declaration order) =
#   target(12) | low(12) | hi(12) | nidx(8) | sib(8 * 32 = 256) | dirs(8)
#   = 308 bytes;  instance = root(32).
.shipshape 1
field GF(2^8) irreducible 0x11B
stdlib crypto-v2

WITNESS  -> %target : byte[12]
WITNESS  -> %low    : byte[12]
WITNESS  -> %hi     : byte[12]
WITNESS  -> %nidx   : byte[8]
WITNESS  -> %sib    : byte[256]
WITNESS  -> %dirs   : byte[8]
INSTANCE -> %root   : byte[32]

stdlib/crypto/indexed_merkle/nonmember_secret[hirose_fixed_32](%target, %low, %hi, %nidx, %sib, %dirs, %root)
